  "configuration_id": "config_028",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 showed scvi_n200 outperforms PCA n2000 by ~3.5 points in the RNA-only setting (0.520 vs 0.485), and config_016 established that the best multimodal result so far (0.527) uses PCA n2000 with ResNet50 and concat fusion. Uncertainty: it is unknown whether the scvi representation advantage persists when image features are also present, since the learned nonlinear latent may interact differently with the concat fusion than a linear PCA projection. This experiment (config_028: multimodal, single profile, scvi_n200, ResNet50, concat) is a clean single-variable swap of the RNA encoder relative to config_016, isolating the encoder effect in the multimodal context. It is the best use of the next budget slot because it directly exploits the strongest evidence we have (scvi > PCA) in the regime where we expect the highest absolute performance, and the outcome will determine which RNA encoder to carry forward into all subsequent multiprofile and fusion-strategy experiments, thereby reducing uncertainty on the most impactful design axis before adding further complexity."
}

